{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q422723","formula":"C₅H₁₂","hill":"C5H12","elements":["H","C"],"composition":{"C":5.0,"H":12.0},"names":{"en":"Neopentane","ru":"Неопентан","uk":"Неопентан"},"descriptions":{"en":"Neopentane, also called 2,2-dimethylpropane, is a double-branched-chain alkane with five carbon atoms, with the chemical formula C(CH3)4. Neopentane is a flammable gas at room temperature and pressure which can condense into a highly volatile liquid on a cold day, in an ice bath, or when compressed to a higher pressure. Neopentane is the simplest alkane with a quaternary carbon, and has achiral tetrahedral symmetry.","ru":"Неопента́н (2,2-диметилпропа́н, тетраметилмета́н) — химическое органическое соединение, относящееся к классу алканов. Химическая формула C(CH3)4. При нормальных условиях — газ.","uk":"Неопентан — диметилпропан, C(CH3)4, ізомер нормального пентану."},"fame":36,"pubchemCid":10041,"mass":72.15,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC(C)(C)C","inchikey":"CRSOQBOWXPBRES-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"2,2-dimethylpropane","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"10041","atoms":17,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.347,"y":0.373,"z":0.636,"el":"C"},{"x":0.896,"y":1.245,"z":-0.068,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.236,"y":-0.538,"z":-1.418,"el":"C"},{"x":0.686,"y":-1.079,"z":0.85,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.211,"y":0.761,"z":1.652,"el":"H"},{"x":-1.862,"y":1.143,"z":0.051,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.01,"y":-0.498,"z":0.699,"el":"H"},{"x":1.867,"y":1.01,"z":-0.518,"el":"H"},{"x":1.083,"y":1.653,"z":0.932,"el":"H"},{"x":0.432,"y":2.035,"z":-0.669,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.874,"y":-1.429,"z":-1.403,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.726,"y":0.211,"z":-2.05,"el":"H"},{"x":0.709,"y":-0.814,"z":-1.9,"el":"H"},{"x":0.868,"y":-0.723,"z":1.87,"el":"H"},{"x":1.652,"y":-1.367,"z":0.42,"el":"H"},{"x":0.0